OL,3,GNEWSARegular spaceplane flights planned
OL,4,Ain project
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpaceplanes could take off on regular
OL,7,Fand possibly daily flights from
OL,8,FCornwall following an agreement.
OL,10,FSpace transport firm Dawn Aerospace and
OL,11,FSpaceport Cornwall have signed a
OL,12,FMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) for a
OL,13,Fproject looking at creating "rapid,
OL,14,Freuseable access to suborbital space"
OL,15,Fin the UK.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F344A1792488352
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSARegular spaceplane flights planned
OL,4,Ain project
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe scheme, known as Dawn Aerospace
OL,7,FSuborbital Horizontal UK Launch
OL,8,FProgramme (Dash UK), would allow Dawn
OL,9,FAerospace's Aurora unmanned 5m (16.4ft)
OL,10,Flong spaceplane to operate from the
OL,11,FSpaceport's base at Cornwall Airport
OL,12,FNewquay, project leaders said.
OL,14,FSpaceport head of engagement Ross
OL,15,FHulbert said the partnership
OL,16,Frepresented an opportunity to bring
OL,17,F"genuinely transformational" aerospace
OL,18,Fcapability.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
